  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "Which of the following is the same as\n\n\\[\\dfrac{2-4+6-8+10-12+14}{3-6+9-12+15-18+21}?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-1\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)",
    "D": "\\(1\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{14}{3}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Pairing adjacent positive and negative terms makes both sums short. The numerator is\n\\[\n(2-4)+(6-8)+(10-12)+14\n=-2-2-2+14=8.\n\\]\nThe denominator is\n\\[\n(3-6)+(9-12)+(15-18)+21\n=-3-3-3+21=12.\n\\]\nSince the denominator is nonzero, the expression equals\n\\[\n\\frac8{12}=\\frac23,\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
